From 09224635a62302efa69fd1e48bdeaa652ff4d51c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arne Juul <arnej@vespa.ai>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 22:32:41 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] Pin the opsets in the custom-registry fp16 fallback tests

Fp16NodeWithCustomRegistryFp16KernelNotForced and
Fp16NodeWithCustomRegistryFp32KernelForcedToFp32 built their models with the
default Model constructor, which imports whatever versions the schema registry
currently reports as latest for every domain. Both tests hinge on a custom
kernel def registered with SinceVersion(1) being found for the node, and an
unbounded kernel def matches Node::SinceVersion() exactly, so a schema revision
landing in either domain would silently stop the lookup from matching and leave
the tests asserting the opposite of what they exist to check. Pin the imports
instead, the way Fp16OutputOnlyNodeWithNoCpuKernelForcedToFp32 already does.

Both domains have to be named, not just ai.onnx: Model uses a non-empty
domain_to_version map verbatim and does not back-fill the domains it omits, so
pinning ai.onnx alone leaves the com.microsoft BiasGelu/BiasAdd nodes with no
opset import.

The versions chosen are the ones in effect today (ai.onnx 12, com.microsoft 1),
so this fixes the tests' opsets in place rather than moving them; behaviour is
unchanged and all 26 TransformerTest cases pass.
